renaissance-cyber: a parallax set for the Neo launcher, the wallpaper of the optional Renaissance look ("Cyberpunk
meets Italian Renaissance"). Drawn by tools/parallax-renaissance/build_renaissance.py from: a granite statue owl of
Minerva (AI generated for the owner with Nano Banana 2.1 on Vertex, 2026-11-14), a gear ring and corner brackets
(same), and Leonardo's Vitruvian Man (public domain, Wikimedia Commons), lifted to line-work and glitch-sliced.

Layers, back to front (depth in parallax.json):
  layer0.jpg  -0.60  OLED night, a cool glow behind the statue, silver dotwork
  layer1.png  -0.25  the gear ring (granite egg-and-dart rim, platinum numerals, gold gears), dimmed
  layer2.png   0.10  the Vitruvian Man in silver line-work, cut into glitch strips, one amber edge
  layer3.png   0.55  the granite owl cut open to platinum, gold wire and gears; Kiroshi camera eyes
  layer4.png   1.00  granite-and-platinum corner brackets, HUD microtext
wallpaper.jpg is the set flattened at rest (1080x2400); preview.jpg is 540x1200.
